practice `$COURSE_SLUG` in vitro: test each claim.
ref: $COURSE_ROUTE/2.2.greats.read.yield.md

in an isolated sandbox (a temp repo or a scratch worktree, never the live tree), build whole,
varied tasks of graded difficulty that could refute each claim. run them. feedback on each run.

give each claim one verdict:
- held — a test could have refuted it, and did not
- refuted — a test refuted it; it stays out of the role's boot
- untested — no test ran

a refuted or untested claim is not the end: return to `2.2.greats.read`, read again for what
was missed, then retest here. stop when each claim holds, or is refuted with the evidence.

emit into $COURSE_ROUTE/3.practice.vitro.yield.md, with this table:

| claim | verdict | evidence |
|---|---|---|
| k1 natural-key upsert dedupes a replay | held | 3 replays, 1 row |
| k7 backoff alone makes a write safe | refuted | 3 replays, 2 duplicate rows |
